# G1 synthetic clearance and subjective burden contract proposal

Status: **UNACCEPTED engineering proposal; no clinical approval, implementation acceptance or runtime evidence.** Author role: Astra/medium, independent of the active structural live-hold implementation. This proposal needs a different independent Astra reviewer and root acceptance before any dependent implementation. Accepted source base: `ec18cb4020ba239710a3fd615e365d5cd72b4d80`. Structural live-hold dependency: accepted plan head `756ce26bf454cce89933439f03572cd34b29eda8`, replacement proposal blob `e6d39d6a0bce37a554cd768e14ee0916edf5da5c`. Its code is neither read nor accepted here. Production checkpoints 9ad/6897 remain held.

## 1. Decision and boundaries

Propose two explicitly synthetic laws: `SIM-REVIEW-01` version 1.0 for offline observed hold/review/resumption trajectories, and `SIM-BURDEN-01` version 1.0 for a fictional patient-reported ordinal support-burden item. Neither law is literature-derived, clinically validated, a clinical safety threshold, or an authorization for real care. Their purpose is to make full G1 producer/evaluator behavior executable and independently checkable where the existing contract lacks definitions.

This document changes no source, parameter, schema, accepted document, ledger or engine. Acceptance would authorize a separately reviewed contract/version integration task, then separately reviewed independent producer and evaluator implementation. The running structural live-hold work must continue to reject absent rule bindings. Its manual review endpoint cannot infer this synthetic law, and an offline simulation principal cannot become an authenticated clinician. `T-OBS2-CLEARANCE-POLICY` closes only for the explicitly registered synthetic archive profile after implementation and evidence; its real-clinician policy remains `CLINICAL-CLEARANCE-01`, unresolved.

