## 10. Remaining gates and handoff

This proposal is complete enough to review the two synthetic definitions and their explicit unresolved dependencies, not to approve clinical use. Required before implementation dispatch: OTHER Astra exact-head/base critique, root acceptance, explicit assignment of contract/version integration owner and independent evaluator ownership. Required before producer acceptance: new canonical/version integration, all script bindings, missingness/likelihood integration, independent finite cases, runtime/boundary/browser evidence and all original G1 compute. Required before burden comparison claims: implemented and verified `BURDEN-PRECISION-01` binding; unresolved components block the complete target. Required before a real clinician clearance claim: `CLINICAL-CLEARANCE-01` and actual clinical/human review, plus implemented authorized workflow.

No runtime tests, generators, calibrations, truth rollouts, browser sessions, clinical reviews or gate transitions were executed for this proposal. The evidence folder records source identities, helper status correction, bounded authoring checks and failed searches/truncated reads. A clean documentation diff or correct arithmetic cannot close full G1, B-OBS2-LIVE-HOLD, scientific, clinical or human gates.
